@startuml serialDriverStateMachine

title Serial Driver - State Machine

state "Uninitialized" as UNINIT
state "Idle" as IDLE
state "TX Busy" as TX_BUSY
state "RX Busy" as RX_BUSY
state "Error" as ERROR

[*] --> UNINIT

UNINIT --> IDLE : Init(pConfig) [valid config] / HAL_UART_Init()
UNINIT --> UNINIT : Any API call / return NOT_INITIALIZED

IDLE --> TX_BUSY : Send(pData, len) [valid params] / HAL_UART_Transmit_IT()
IDLE --> RX_BUSY : Receive(pData, maxLen) [valid params] / HAL_UART_Receive_IT()
IDLE --> UNINIT : DeInit() / HAL_UART_DeInit()
IDLE --> IDLE : Configure() [valid params] / update config
IDLE --> IDLE : GetStatus() / return current status

TX_BUSY --> IDLE : TX_Complete_Callback() / invoke txCallback
TX_BUSY --> ERROR : TX_Error_Callback() / invoke error handling
TX_BUSY --> IDLE : Timeout elapsed / return TIMEOUT
TX_BUSY --> TX_BUSY : Send() / return BUSY

RX_BUSY --> IDLE : RX_Complete_Callback() / invoke rxCallback, store data
RX_BUSY --> ERROR : RX_Error_Callback() / invoke error handling
RX_BUSY --> IDLE : Timeout elapsed / return TIMEOUT
RX_BUSY --> RX_BUSY : Receive() / return BUSY

ERROR --> IDLE : Init(pConfig) / re-initialize HAL
ERROR --> UNINIT : DeInit() / HAL_UART_DeInit()

note right of TX_BUSY
  DMA or Interrupt-driven transmission.
  Buffer pointer and length tracked internally.
end note

note right of RX_BUSY
  DMA or Interrupt-driven reception.
  Data written directly to caller-provided buffer.
end note

note right of ERROR
  Overrun, framing, parity, or noise error detected.
  Requires re-initialization to recover.
end note

@enduml
